# Multi-agent coordination that does not happen
#
# The same three people, the same shared goal, the same runtime.  The only
# difference from `coordination.catharsis` is the state of the trust graph.
#
# In the working version Alice has enough hope to move first, and the gratitude
# her contributions produce raises everyone else's trust until they join in.
# Here nobody can move first, so the gratitude that would have unlocked the
# others is never generated, and the group sits at nearly zero forever.
#
# That is the whole point: coordination is not a feature of the runtime, it is a
# fixed point of the relationships.  You can lose it by editing the feelings.

group rescue_team

agent alice bob charlie

join alice rescue_team
join bob rescue_team
join charlie rescue_team

goal rescue_team "rescue"

doubt alice bob 0.6
doubt bob charlie 0.6
doubt charlie alice 0.6

fear alice 0.5
fear bob 0.5
pride charlie 0.7

tick 20

observe rescue_team
